  "guide": {"focus":"Follow the contact forces through the stack as the boxes settle and come to rest.","predict":{"prompt":"After making the lowest box heavier, will the upper boxes fall through it?","options":["No, the stack remains supported","Yes, they fall through","The lowest box rises"]},"variables":[{"control":"object.properties.mass","label":"Lowest box mass","body":"body-1-2"}],"steps":[{"text":"Run until the boxes stop moving and the stack has settled."},{"text":"Increase the lowest box's mass, press R, and watch how the stack responds.","control":"object.properties.mass","body":"body-1-2"},{"text":"Open Collisions to inspect the impacts recorded as the boxes settled.","open":"measure.collisions.list"}],"expect":"Contacts support the stack. Once the boxes stay below the motion thresholds long enough, they go to sleep and remain supported.","limits":"The boxes are perfectly rigid. Speed and time thresholds determine when they can be treated as resting."},
